>>Prediction:- depends on training data  ,prompt, temperature(Creativity), max token length.Tokens with highest probabloty is not always chosen , thats because of sampling strategies & decoding settings like :- temp , top p , top k , min p )
>Sampling parameters (Settings):-These control how the model selects tokens while generating a response.Think of them as knobs you adjust when using the model, without retraining it.Examples: Temperature, Top-K, Top-P and Min-P.
   Temperature :-Controls how sharply or evenly probabilities are distributed during sampling.controls randomness
     Low temperature: more predictable choices, almost always pick the top most token, strong peak probablity distribution.
     High temperature: more diverse choices,weak peak probablity distribution.
   Top-K:-Keeps only the K highest-ranked candidate tokens before sampling.
     Ex-Top-K = 3 means sampling among the three highest-ranked candidates.
   Top-P (nucleus sampling):- Keeps the smallest set of highest-probability tokens whose cumulative probability reaches the chosen threshold.
     Ex-let Top-P = 0.90 ,then keeps a candidate set covering approximately 90% of the probability mass.
   Min-P :-Removes tokens whose probability is too low relative to the highest-probability token.
     Example: Min-P = 0.1, then calculate 10% of the highest token's probability, then remove token less then that relative cutoff.


